,"distance":0.1701,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"},{"season":2023,"team":"CIN","distance":0.1874,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2022,"team":"CHI","distance":0.2229,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"GB","distance":0.2292,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"SEA","distance":0.2431,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Dolphins are 1-8 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 224 to 148. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 25th in EPA per play and the defense 27th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits are the lowest pass rate over expected and the 2nd fewest pass rushers in the league.","offense":"The Dolphins offense has been well below average by EPA per play so far. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 3rd highest pre-snap motion rate and the 2nd most backs in the backfield in the league. Malik Willis has run the passing game, with Malik Washington leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Dolphins have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 27th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, EPA allowed per rush, only ranks 21st, and it is 31st in success rate allowed. Chop Robinson leads the team with 5 sacks, and Joshua Uche has added 3, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they have the 2nd fewest pass rushers in the league.","special":"The Dolphins have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 57% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 68% of field goals, which is one of the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 11% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Malik Willis has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,396 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Malik Washington and Caleb Douglas leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Ollie Gordon II has handled most of the work in the backfield with 64% of the carries. On defense, Chop Robinson leads the team with 5 sacks and Michael Taaffe has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Bobby Slowik is calling the offense and Sean Duggan is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 49ers under Kyle Shanahan and the 2024 Ravens under Todd Monken. Their defense looks most like the 2022 Saints under Dennis Allen and the 2023 Bengals under Lou Anarumo.","trends":"The offense went from 22nd in EPA per play in 2025 to 25th so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 26th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 27th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was fourth down go rate, which went from 18% to 57%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}